# ALPHANET: the Foundation's LIVE public staging network.
# networkID: 21337 on the running chain (collides with Xahau Mainnet);
# moves to 24100 at the next genesis reset. network/settings.mk NETWORK_ID is the source of truth.
# DNS record (xrpl.org zone):
#   alphanet.xrpl.org         -> 79.110.60.105  (Cloudflare proxied, zone mode Full)
#     Public clients use wss://alphanet.xrpl.org and https://alphanet.xrpl.org on 443.
#     Cloudflare does not proxy 6018/5017, so those origin nginx ports work only direct
#     to the IP, not through the hostname. The old *.nerdnest.xyz names are gone.
#   rpc.alphanet.xrpl.org     -> 79.110.60.105  (DNS-only)
#   faucet.alphanet.xrpl.org  -> 79.110.60.105  (DNS-only)
#   vl.alphanet.xrpl.org      -> 79.110.60.105  (DNS-only; publisher list + Let's Encrypt cert,
#                                                auto-renewing, nginx reload via deploy hook)
# KNOWN GAP: the list is served off pnode1, the same host as the public endpoint, so halting
# .105 in a drill also stops VL refresh. Moving it to pnode2 removes that shared failure mode.
# Column 3 is the node name: it names the per-node drill key ($SSH_KEY_DIR/<name>) and
# the monitoring `node` label, so both line up with the ansible node names.
VALIDATOR 79.110.60.99  vnode1
VALIDATOR 79.110.60.100 vnode2
VALIDATOR 79.110.60.101 vnode3
VALIDATOR 79.110.60.102 vnode4
VALIDATOR 79.110.60.103 vnode5
VALIDATOR 79.110.60.104 vnode6
PEER      79.110.60.105 pnode1
PEER      79.110.60.106 pnode2
# Operator break-glass key, on every node. Never handed out.
SSH_KEY   ~/.ssh/xrpl-labs
# Per-node drill keys live here as <node name>; one per node so a drill participant can be
# given exactly one node and revoked without rotating anyone else.
SSH_KEY_DIR ~/.ssh/alphanet
SSH_PORT  1988
SSH_USER  root
# Publisher list the nodes fetch. Signed by the alphanet publisher key in the cluster keystore.
# http, not https: the blob is verified against [validator_list_keys], so integrity does not come
# from TLS. The node containers ship no CA bundle and run [ssl_verify] 0, so https would add a
# handshake and a failure mode while verifying nothing. The hostname also serves https for
# browsers and external tooling.
VL_SITE   http://vl.alphanet.xrpl.org/vl.json
